# POLICY CHANGED 2026-07-29 after two container rollbacks destroyed hours of streaming.
#
# Previously this ignored *.csv so a half-written table could never be committed looking complete. That
# reasoning was sound and the cost turned out to be higher: the rollbacks took every in-progress table with
# them, while the tables that had been committed on completion survived untouched.
#
# Feature tables are now committed freely, INCLUDING partial ones, because incompleteness is already
# machine-checkable without a naming convention: every table has a sidecar <table>.manifest.json, and the
# runner reports n_in_shard against the row count. A reader can tell. A destroyed table cannot be read at all.
#
# Still never committed: raw EEG, credentials, anything patient-identifying.
*.edf
*.eeg
*.vhdr
*.vmrk
*.mat
*.dat
